---
description: Ignore accidental "clear" messages
alwaysApply: true
---

# Ignore "clear"

When the user sends only **"clear"** (or "Clear"), treat it as a mistaken/accidental message (e.g. they meant to clear their terminal, not to ask the AI).

- Do **not** run the `clear` command or take any action.
- Reply briefly, e.g. "No action taken. If you meant to clear your terminal, run `clear` there (or Cmd+K)."
